# Equalize surviving token frequencies (held-out spec FB-0441).
# expect: 12 3 5
# Input tokens, with their original multiplicities.
list
  2 5 8 11 14 17 17 14 11 8 5 2 5 8 11 14 17 17 14 11 14 17 11 17 14 17 17
end let tokens

# Collect distinct values, then count each in the original list.
empty let distinct
tokens each
  let token
  distinct token contains not if
    distinct token push let distinct
  then
end
list distinct each tokens swap count end end let frequencies

# For fixed f, retain f copies of every value with at least f copies.
# Ascending candidates and strict improvement preserve the smallest f.
0 let best-kept
0 let best-frequency
0 let best-distinct
1 frequencies largest 1 add range each
  let frequency
  0 frequencies each frequency ge if 1 add then end let survivors
  frequency survivors mul let kept
  kept best-kept gt if
    kept let best-kept
    frequency let best-frequency
    survivors let best-distinct
  then
end

tokens len best-kept sub
best-frequency
best-distinct
